@tonyabbott, would you be willing to create minimal project that demonstrates the behavior you are witnessing?

That would be extremely helpful to the team in terms of investigating what's going on!

Either a PR for this repository or a separate project in your own public repository would suffice.

@tonyabbott, thanks for the sample project!

I can confirm that this is a bug.

We'll look into it!

@tonyabbott, with the help of your example project and a bit of class loading magic, I've been able to reproduce the failure in a test:

```java
@Test
void findNestedClassesWithBrokenNestedClass() throws Exception {
	URL jarfile = getClass().getResource("/gh-1436-groovy-broken-class-file.jar");

	try (URLClassLoader classLoader = new URLClassLoader(new URL[] { jarfile })) {
		String className = "tests.NestedInterfaceGroovyTests";
		Class<?> classWithBrokenClassFile = classLoader.loadClass(className);

		assertEquals(className, classWithBrokenClassFile.getName());
		NoClassDefFoundError noClassDefFoundError = assertThrows(NoClassDefFoundError.class,
			() -> classWithBrokenClassFile.getDeclaredClasses());
		assertEquals("tests/NestedInterfaceGroovyTests$NestedInterface$1", noClassDefFoundError.getMessage());

		assertThat(ReflectionUtils.findNestedClasses(classWithBrokenClassFile, clazz -> true)).isEmpty();
	}
}
```

So that'll make it easier to fix (and know it's fixed). 😉
